<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00504</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a2842dd2-e8bd-49d3-a045-326e0b7e39d2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 2, use the following passage:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A runner is training for a marathon. She runs more than 4 days each week. Each day, she runs between 12 and 15 miles. The marathon is 3 months away at the most.</para>
</blockquote>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="b3d7a0ad-9894-431b-a9f9-d57f1138e170" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0ca15f01-7b3c-49e2-a528-491f804852e2" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the number of days the runner runs each week" data-solution-options="[&quot;the number of miles in a marathon&quot;, &quot;the number of miles the runner runs each day&quot;, &quot;the number of months away the marathon is&quot;, &quot;the number of days the runner runs each week&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What does the inequality \(d &gt; 4\) represent? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! the number of days the runner runs each week</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5de3c9b4-ffc9-49f9-86b6-f512ceaeb3bb" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the number of miles the runner runs each day" data-solution-options="[&quot;the number of miles in a marathon&quot;, &quot;the number of miles the runner runs each day&quot;, &quot;the number of months away the marathon is&quot;, &quot;the number of days the runner runs each week&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What does the inequality \(12\;\leq\;m\;\leq\;15\) represent? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! the number of miles the runner runs each day</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>For 3 - 8, write an inequality to represent the constraint given. </para>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="525ef5e7-cfc5-46d2-8b91-0e0b8c1c308b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04452122-a496-4774-88f1-f37f209b48b8" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(p &lt; 4 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(p &lt; 4 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p &gt; 4 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p\\;\\leq\\;4\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p\\;\\geq\\;4\\;\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> There are less than 4 patients, \(p\), in the waiting room. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(p\;&lt;\;4\;\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a25872c8-fc00-4da6-af27-9ea7337fd151" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(c\;\leq\;6 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(c &gt; 6 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c\\;\\leq\\;6 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c &lt; 6 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c\\;\\geq\\;6\\;\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> There are no more than 6 cats, \(c\), in the yard. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( c ≤ 6 \)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3f993c8d-6884-4bbb-8604-aa21aba0598c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(m\;\geq\;7\;\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(m &gt; 7 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m\\;\\leq\\;7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m &lt; 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m\\;\\geq\\;7\\;\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> There are no less than 7 markers, \(m\), in the drawer. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(m\;\geq\;7\;\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
</div>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d84391bb-fb81-49d6-a707-6ee13cba663b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="21948567-9795-45ab-ba5c-d269cd4e7474" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(12\;≤\;e\;≤\;19\;\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(12 &gt; e\\) and \\(\\;e\\;\\;&gt;\\;19\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(12\\;\\geq\\;e\\;\\)and\\(\\;e\\;\\geq\\;19\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(e\\;\\leq\\;19\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(12\\;≤\\;e\\;≤\\;19\\;\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> The basket has between 12 and 19 eggs, \(e\). </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(12 ≤ e ≤ 19 \)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
