</div>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="bdf70601-cfb8-4dca-b4b8-4b1c1bc48aea" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="57a2b48e-e646-40cd-a130-2bda02cb8b94" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(8a + 3c &gt; 68 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(8a\\;+\\;3c\\;\\leq\\;68\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(8a\\;+\\;3c\\;\\geq\\;68\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(8a + 3c &lt; 68 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(8a + 3c &gt; 68 \\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> The total sales of tickets to a show is more than $68. An adult ticket, <emphasis effect="italics">a</emphasis>, costs $8 and a children’s ticket, \(c\), is $3. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(8a + 3c &gt; 68 \)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="40ce7a53-87d6-4d8c-9da5-f411619fb487" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(c\;\geq\;\frac s4\;\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(c\\;\\geq\\;\\frac s4\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c\\;&gt;\\;\\frac s4\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c\\;&lt;\\;\\frac s4\\;\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c\\;\\leq\\;\\frac s4\\;\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> There needs to be at least 1 pound of clay, \(c\), for every 4 students, \(s\). </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(c\;\geq\;\frac s4\;\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>For 9 - 11, use the following passage: </para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A doctor sees between 7 and 12 patients each day. On Mondays and Tuesdays, the
    appointment times are 15 minutes. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, they are 30 minutes long. On Fridays, they are one hour long. The doctor works for no more than 8 hours a day. Here are some inequalities that represent this situation. </para>
</blockquote>
<para>\(0.25\;\leq\;y\;\leq\;1\)            \(7\;\leq\;x\;\leq\;12\)           \(xy\;\leq\;8\)</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d98f6c9d-f47a-437f-9e52-e9b0b337ed64" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="80586fbc-b2d8-421d-acc7-0fadf313b894" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the number of patients the doctor sees each day." data-solution-options="[&quot;the number of patients the doctor sees each day.&quot;, &quot;the part of an hour that each appointment lasts.&quot;, &quot;the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day.&quot;, &quot;the number of patients the doctor sees in a week.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What does the variable <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis> represent? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! the number of patients the doctor sees each day</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c8c68be2-5987-4311-bc26-ec6a58774d65" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the part of an hour that each appointment lasts." data-solution-options="[&quot;the number of patients the doctor sees each day.&quot;, &quot;the part of an hour that each appointment lasts.&quot;, &quot;the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day.&quot;, &quot;the number of patients the doctor sees in a week.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What does the variable <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis> represent? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! the part of an hour that each appointment lasts</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="52e5dd2c-2137-4963-ad5b-91a7f20a4320" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day." data-solution-options="[&quot;the number of patients the doctor sees each day.&quot;, &quot;the part of an hour that each appointment lasts.&quot;, &quot;the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day.&quot;, &quot;the number of patients the doctor sees in a week.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What does the expression \(xy\) in the last inequality mean in this situation? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>For 12 - 14, use the following passage:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>Arnav wants to build a dog house. He makes a list of the materials needed:</para>
  <list>
    <item>At least 60 square feet of plywood for the surfaces</item>
    <item>At least 36 feet of wood planks for the frame of the dog house </item>
    <item>Between 1 and 2 quarts of paint</item>
  </list>
  <para>Arnav's budget is $65. Plywood costs $0.70 per square foot, planks of wood cost $0.10 per foot, and paint costs $8 per quart.</para>
</blockquote>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="afc61e84-1ad5-4471-90d8-51957ee60aad" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q12-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bc2297ed-28d8-428f-b938-3a65cf880bf6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="\(p\;\geq\;60\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(p\\;\\geq\\;60\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p\\;\\geq\\;36\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(1\\;\\leq\\;p\\;\\leq\\;2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which inequality represents the square feet of plywood needed? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(p\;\geq\;60\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q13-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ab779033-04ec-4745-95d6-404d192cfdf3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="\(w\;\geq\;36\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(w\\;\\geq\\;60\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(1\\;\\leq\\;w\\;\\leq\\;2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(w\\;\\geq\\;36\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which inequality represents the number of wood planks needed? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(w\;\geq\;36\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q14-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b2f185f1-5900-4c03-b982-b2d373c39ad9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="\(1\;\leq\;q\;\leq\;2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(q\\;\\geq\\;60\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(1\\;\\leq\\;q\\;\\leq\\;2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(q\\;\\geq\\;36\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which inequality represents the number of quarts of paint needed? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(1\;\leq\;q\;\leq\;2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.8.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
